WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.080
Good morning, Hank! It's Tuesday

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:03.700
And in a stirring turn of events I find myself in an airport.

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:06.880
I'm on my way to Davos, Switzerland for the World Economic Forum

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:11.900
which is a gathering of like world leaders and CEOs and Leonardo DiCaprio and I guess... me?

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:13.920
to discuss the future of the world's economy.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:20.440
I'm not even there yet and I already feel a little out of place BUT Davos, Switzerland was also the setting of one of my all-time favorite novels

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:22.040
The Magic Mountain by Thomas Mann

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:26.720
so while I'm there I get to do a bit of literary tourism which, as you know, Hank, is one of my three favorite hobbies.

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:31.100
My favorite hobbies, of course, being: eating pizza, sponsoring 4th tier soccer teams and literary tourism.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.140
Anyway, Hank, you can follow my trip  to Davos on my Twitter or Instagram or SnapChat

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:38.140
I don't actually know how to log on to my SnapChat but I'm going to try to figure it out!

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:41.060
All of that, however, is an aside because it's Tuesday! It's Question Tuesday

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:44.520
the day that I answer real questions from real Nerdfighters. Let's belatedly get right to it!

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:45.460
How's the writing going?

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:47.660
I think it's going well, I'm sorry it's taking so long.

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:49.440
Hey, what's going to be the title of your new book?

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:53.680
I don't know, you got any ideas?  I'm defintely in the market for a good title so if you have one leave it in comments!

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:55.400
What is your opinion of inside jokes?

00:00:55.400 --> 00:01:01.120
*Joyful shouting by the Cheez Doodles Guy*

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:02.420
Who are you going to vote for presi-

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:05.560
Nononono I am not paying attention to the so-called

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:10.260
"Presidential Election" until 100 days before the primary in my home state of Indiana

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:14.420
Which means I have a few more blessed days not to think about it and I am going to enjoy them.

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:16.220
Will you be my friend even though I'm a Slytherin?

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:19.580
Yeah sure! Hufflepuffs are kind and caring and open...

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:21.120
Unlike some people I know...

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:23.180
Can you six degrees of Kevin Bacon yourself?

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:25.040
Yeah! I acted in The Fault in Our Stars movie

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:29.120
Admittedly, my scene was cut but it was in the extended version! I acted with Laura Dern

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:31.680
who was in Novocaine with Kevin Bacon.

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:33.340
How should a dog wear pants?

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:36.300
When it comes to dogs with pants, I stand with the president.

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:39.840
At this point do presidential debates actually accomplish what they're supposed to accomplish?

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:45.860
Well, as far as I can tell at this point, what they're supposed to accomplish is selling lots of extra expensive advertising on Cable news networks

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:47.980
In which case, yeah - they're very effective!

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:49.560
How do you think the world will end?

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:52.440
Well, I've got a list of my top ten eschatological anxieties

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:54.820
but in the end I'm with T.S. Eliot on this one.

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:56.880
"Not with a bang but with a whimper."

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:59.260
When is Looking for Alaska gonna be made into a movie?

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:02.340
Uhhhhhh.... I don't know. Maybe never?

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:07.980
I sold the movie rights to a movie studio more than ten years ago and I have tried many, many, many times

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:10.100
to buy them back in the intervening decade.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:15.620
But thus far that hasn't happened. They tried to make a movie a bunch of times but it's always fallen apart for one reason or another.

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:19.940
And at this point, uh... I'm not involved in the project in any way.

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:25.300
I'm not gonna lie, it definitely bums me out but it also reminds me just how lucky I was to have two amazing

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:27.140
book-to-movie experiences

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:31.880
The truth is authors are almost never as welcomed into the process as I was with The Fault in Our Stars and Paper Towns

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:34.220
So... I try just to be grateful for that.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:37.520
So if you don't hear Looking for Alaska movie updates from me that's why.

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:39.740
Uhh... maybe that will change some day - I hope so!

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:41.840
But, uh, I don't expect so.

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:43.600
Any plans to come back to Crash Course?

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:46.460
Yes! This summer we're gonna do another mini-series of Crash Course: Literature

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:50.960
We're gonna read Huckleberry Finn and Invisible Man and One Hundred Years of Solitude and Their Eyes Were Watching God

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:53.400
and some Shakespearean sonnets. It's gonna be AMAZING!

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:54.680
Who's your celebrity crush?

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:56.580
Right now I'd definitely say Lin Manuel Miranda

00:02:56.580 --> 00:03:00.520
Is there a smell that is important to you and brings you back to a particular time in your life?

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:03.600
Yeah there's an odor of like spray smell called "Spring Rain"

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:08.180
that brings me back to high school because it's what my roommate and I always used to cover up the smell of cigarette smoke.

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:13.720
Obviously, don't smoke. It's a tremendous waste of time and money but that Spring Rain odor brings me right back to high school.

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:17.940
It's like this horrific, horrific scent but it only makes me feel happy.

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:22.660
Alright, Hank, I have to go board the plane. Next week, I'll give you some thoughts from Davos. In the meantime, I will see you on Friday!

